--- 02:13 UTC pre-launch clarification of the H1 instrument (still before launch; nothing has run):
the harness-injected message carries the command's OUTPUT plus the tool's "[exit code: N]" line, never the
command itself (loop.py _try_harness_verify; bash.py appends the exit line). Importing a library prints
nothing, so an import-form verify shows a bare "[exit code: 0]" body; -m on the cycle-importing package
shows the runpy RuntimeWarning. H1 therefore reads: NEW-arm harness messages carry no RuntimeWarning and
(when the module prints nothing at import) a bare exit-code body; OLD-arm messages are expected to carry
the RuntimeWarning when the harness ran. The build under test is positively controlled by the recipe.py
sha256 the chain prints at every swap: old a2bd86df2301, new 571b595aa176 (staged on zc-01 at 02:13).
